    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two matched-cycle trace-Jacobi norm transfer",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On the matched c=0 two-antipodal-denominator generic cycle branch at M=2^36, the Chebyshev/Gegenbauer sign router gives six exact trace gcds per fixed epsilon, and the even-Jacobi quadratic norm reduces each packet coverage-equivalently from degree at most 2^37 to degree at most 2^36. Thus the complete interface has two six-gcd packets and at most twelve signed branches. The torsion-only prefilter is one cyclotomic norm at order 2^39 for epsilon=-1 and a 37-level tower at orders 2^2 through 2^38 for epsilon=1; equivalent trace and quadratic-minus splits have maximum degree 2^36. A compatible divisor is only a candidate and must still pass the signed norm and corrected T/q_out fourth-power gate. No norm is evaluated and no large run is authorized.",
